    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311-a2">

                <pb facs="0599" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg473"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Alfaro</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">South</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1925.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">S. P. No. 262</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: With reference to our interview of
                    this morning permit me to inform Your Excellency that the Government of Panama
                    considers that in order to proceed with the nomination of the <pb facs="0600"
                        n="474" xml:id="pg474"/> Panaman engineer who should participate in the
                    demarcation of the boundary line with Costa Rica, it is essential that a
                    previous agreement be reached along the lines indicated in the note which I had
                    the honor to address to Your Excellency dated the 29th instant, numbered S. P.
                    249.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. J. Alfaro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
